{"name":"Vulcanised","hex":"#424443","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vulcanised","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of vulcanise"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vulcanised"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vulcanization","blocks":[{"text":"Vulcanization is a range of processes for hardening rubbers. The term originally referred exclusively to the treatment of natural rubber with sulfur and heat, which remains the most common practice. It has also grown to include the hardening of other (synthetic) rubbers via various means. Examples include silicone rubber via room temperature vulcanising and chloroprene rubber (neoprene) using metal oxides."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/VulcanizationMold1941.jpg/330px-VulcanizationMold1941.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vulcanization"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Roller-hockey-%28Quad%29-Ball.jpg/500px-Roller-hockey-%28Quad%29-Ball.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Roller-hockey-%28Quad%29-Ball.jpg/1280px-Roller-hockey-%28Quad%29-Ball.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Roller-hockey-%28Quad%29-Ball.jpg/500px-Roller-hockey-%28Quad%29-Ball.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roller hockey ball created via vulcanization","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoller-hockey-(Quad)-Ball.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/The_Employment_of_Women_in_Britain%2C_1914-1918_Q28267.jpg/500px-The_Employment_of_Women_in_Britain%2C_1914-1918_Q28267.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t